<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">talents</ansi>

A talent is a small, permanent bonus you choose at levels 5, 15, 25, 35, 45
and 55. Each lineage has its own list of five. You may take the same talent
twice, unless it says it can be taken once.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Commands</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">talent</ansi>                          your talents and any you may still choose
  <ansi fg="command">talent list</ansi>                     your lineage's talents
  <ansi fg="command">talent pick [talent]</ansi>            preview a choice
  <ansi fg="command">talent pick [talent] confirm</ansi>    take it (permanent)
  <ansi fg="command">talent pick [member] [talent]</ansi>   the same for a companion

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The lists</ansi>

  Cleric   Mending Hands (+10% healing), Steadfast Prayer (blows break your
           chant 25% less often), Deep Well (+10% maximum mana), Sanctuary
           (+3 Evasion while chanting), Gentle Rest (after-battle patching
           costs 15% less mana)
  Warrior  Toughness (+8% maximum health), Heavy Hands (+1 damage on every
           blow), Keen Edge (+2 Attack), Footwork (+2 Evasion), Tackle Drill
           (Tackle ready a round sooner; once)
  Samurai  Keen Edge, Footwork, Heavy Hands, Toughness, Sharp Eye (+3% critical
           chance on every blow)
  Witch    Deep Well, Steadfast Prayer, Thrift (spells cost 10% less mana),
           Potent Hex (+5 to a hex's chance to land), Sanctuary
  Wizard   Deep Well, Focus (+8% spell damage), Steadfast Prayer, Thrift,
           Sanctuary
  Ranger   Keen Edge, Footwork, Steady Aim (Aimed Shot +2 damage), Quick Draw
           (Aimed Shot ready a round sooner; once), Toughness
  Halberdier  Toughness, Heavy Hands, Keen Edge, Footwork, Sweep Drill (Sweep ready
           a round sooner; once)
  Rogue    Keen Edge, Footwork, Deep Cuts (Opening Strike +2 damage), Patient
           Hand (Opening Strike ready a round sooner; once), Heavy Hands

Talents need no class: a character can take its first at level 5, before
promotion. Picks beyond what your level has earned stay on your record but do
nothing until you have earned the slot.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help progression</ansi>.
